TEXT: The account's proposed test - see whether two or three concretely specified chores stop recurring - does not distinguish the ambiguity hypothesis from the alternatives. Load imbalance or resentment can coexist with reduced friction on specified items, and recurrence may reappear as new complaint items or after the next schedule change.
BEARING: Weakens the claim that falling recurrence would confirm c1 and rising recurrence would refute it; the test has lower discriminating power than the account implies.
